{"n": 1075, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "1075.webp", "text": "54-29\n\nELECTRIC / HYDRAULIC CONVERTIBLE TOP\nDescription:\n\nit is only possible to operate the top In a stopped car and with the ignition on, and\nOperation lasts only as long as the operating switch In the dashboard Is pressed.\n\nThe switch Is Iiluminated when lights are switched on.\n\nAll windows must be wound down and the trunk lid closed.\n\nIf the car Is moved off with an unlocked top, the top will be run back Into the top box (not\nwhen the top lid Is already locked).\n\nA_Opening Top\n\n1) Unlock and lift top past the TDC point (manual)\n2) Operate top switch in “open” direction\n(until opening movement Is completed)\n\n3) Fold up‘tensioning bar (automatic)\n4) Unlock top lid (automatic)\n5) Open top lid (automatic)\n6) Lower tensioning bar (automatic)\n7) Run in top (automatic)\n8) Close top lid (automatic)\n9) Lock top Ild (automatic)\n8 Closing Top\n\n1) Operate top switch in “close” direction\n(until closing movement Is compieted)\n\n2) Unlock top lid (automatic)\n3) Open top lid (automatic)\n4) Run out top (automatic)\n5) Fold up tensioning bar (automatic)\n6) Close top lid (automatic)\n7) Lock top lid (automatic)\n8) Lower tensioning bar (automatic)\n9) Pull top past the TDC point and lock (automatic)\n\nPump and valves are operated by the electronic control unit in accordance with operation\nand position of the top. Pressure Is bullt up In the operating cylinders, piston rods are\nrun out or In and move the top or top lid via cinematics.\n\nAn Indicator lamp in the Instrument cléuster sends Information to the driver with the\nignition turned on.\n\n1) On Continuously: During top operation ((switch pressed - top moving)\n\n2) Continuous Flashing: Don't move off!\nThe final locked position of the top has not been reached\n(locking lever on cowl panel and/or top lid not closed).\n\n3) Off: One of the top’s final locked positions has been reached\n(locked or top lid closed).", "words": [["5